{"id":"chatcmpl-1fc3e96a-9ea9-48ea-a651-ad5f57ffac9d","object":"chat.completion","created":1795251362,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation when initial findings are ambiguous or contradictory. The approach uses multiple specialized vision-language models to independently assess the same image, then resolves discrepancies through targeted region-of-interest zooming and expert re-querying. Laterality determination on lateral views requires inferring 3D position from 2D trajectory cues relative to anatomical landmarks.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When two independent image-analysis models disagree on a finding, escalate to a third targeted query with more specific anatomical framing rather than accepting either result.\",\n    \"For spatial laterality questions on lateral/projection views, ask models to describe trajectory relative to fixed anatomical landmarks (spine, sternum) before requesting a side determination.\",\n    \"Use region-of-interest cropping and zoom to visually confirm ambiguous structures before committing to a final interpretation.\",\n    \"Chain specialized expert models sequentially: first for presence detection, then for localization, then for laterality inference, rather than asking one model everything at once.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Decompose the question into presence, location, and laterality sub-queries; use multiple VLMs for cross-validation; zoom into ambiguous regions; rely on anatomical landmark relationships for spatial reasoning.\",\n    \"Multi-model consensus tasks\": \"When models disagree, don't average or pick arbitrarily—re-query with sharper, more constrained prompts that force the model to reason from specific evidence.\",\n    \"Spatial reasoning from 2D projections\": \"Convert laterality/side questions into trajectory-relative-to-landmark questions; anatomical context (spine vs sternum) disambiguates projection ambiguity.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding's presence with at least two independent models or one model plus visual ROI zoom before answering.\",\n    \"For laterality questions, verify the model justified its side choice using anatomical landmark trajectory, not just a guess.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":632,"total_tokens":1036,"completion_tokens":404,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":632},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":404}}}